.TH NTSC 1 "August 2026" "ntsc" "NTSC Manual"
.SH NAME
ntsc \- the Neutron Type-Safe Compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ntsc
.RI <command> " [" options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ntsc
is a statically typed, memory-safe systems language compiler that produces
native binaries through LLVM. It pairs a compact, readable syntax with
compiler-enforced ownership: values move by default, borrows are declared
with
.BR view ,
and memory is released deterministically when ownership ends.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init " [name]"
Scaffold a new project with a
.I build.ntbl
manifest and a
.I src/main.nt
entry point.
.TP
.B build " [--release]"
Compile the project to
.I build/debug/
or
.I build/release/.
.TP
.B test " [--release]"
Discover and run
.I test
blocks.
.TP
.B run " [--release]"
Build and execute the project.
.TP
.B clean
Remove the
.I build/
directory.
.TP
.B watch " [--release]"
Rebuild whenever sources change.
.TP
.B graph
Print the module dependency graph in DOT format.
.TP
.B version
Print detailed version information and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-release
Build in release mode with the LLVM optimization pipeline.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Build in debug mode (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit diagnostics as JSON on standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-help , \-h
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version , \-V
Print the compiler version, LLVM revision, host triple, build profile, and
git commit, then exit.
.SH VERSION
The package version identifies the release this binary was built from.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <prefix>/lib/ntsc/libntsc_runtime.a
The runtime static library that
.B ntsc build
links every NTSC program against.
.B ntsc
locates it relative to its own executable: beside the binary, or in the sibling
.I lib/ntsc
(Debian, Arch, tarball) or
.I lib64/ntsc
(Fedora) directory. The portable
.I .tar.gz
archives keep it in
.IR lib/ntsc .
.SH SEE ALSO
The user guide and language reference are available in the repository under
.IR docs/ .
